Richard and Veronica,

I moved the staged changeover into the lead after Veronica's read. The attach=
ed Word draft is v0.3 of ACN-INV-20260114-DRF-001. The separate workbook, ACN=
-INV-20260113-LOG-001, has all nine quotes. Three are comparable on price. Q0=
3 is $500 below Q01 on that basis.

Could you mark any sentence that gives the reader the impression the committe=
e or council adopted the staff's reasoning? The March 13 evaluation at releas=
e page 64 supports saying staff recommended Q01 because its written sequence =
called for keeping a terminal available during replacement. For Q03, the revi=
ew records what staff could establish from the papers they had. I'm keeping t=
hat distinction in the lead.

The March 18 committee minutes for item 4 and the April 8 council minutes for=
 purchasing item 7B are both still pending under the January 12 follow-up, AC=
N-INV-20260112-REQ-001. I can place the matter on both agendas. The paragraph=
s on committee deliberation and council action stay on hold until we have the=
ir respective records.

Thanks,
Leslie

